<title>USA: Amerijet launches twice-weekly service to Aruba.</title>
<headline>Amerijet launches twice-weekly service to Aruba.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amerijet International Inc on Tuesday began twice-weekly scheduled air cargo service between Miami and Aruba, the company said.</p>
<p>Service will be Tuesday and Thursdays initially and is likely to be increased as customer demand rises, Amerijet said in a news release.</p>
<p>With the addition of Aruba to its schedule, Amerijet now ferries cargo to 18 Caribbean destinations, as well as 16 other destinatons in the Americas, with a fleet of Boeing Co 727-200 and 727-100 aircraft.</p>
<p>-- Miami newsroom, ((305-374-5013))</p>
